      },
      "transcript": "What people normally want in life is exactly what they don't know. Knowing exactly what you want sometimes can be really tricky, especially if you're going through a crisis. If I had had a clear idea of what I wanted and where I wanted to go, it would have been a lot easier for me when I was younger. Nevertheless, I think that having this type of crisis in your life makes you stronger, once you've overcome them. Developing skills does not only require dedication, but sometimes they come from hardships. You live and teach you some things you would never learn by listening to others' experiences. To be a grown-up has never been only a matter of age, but something that comes with the different moments lived in life.",
